+++ b/tizen-campaign-kb/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+---
+name: tizen-campaign-kb
+description: Query, import and synchronize Clang campaign repair precedents in an external JSONL knowledge base. Use for offline repair reuse and audit, not for compilation, QuickBuild submission or review approval.
+---
+
+# Tizen Campaign Knowledge Base
+
+## Inputs And Commands
+
+Keep `kb_db` as an absolute JSONL path outside the repository. All writers use
+its sibling `.lock`; do not edit records while a command is running.
+
+```bash
+python -m tizen_campaign_kb kb query --db /work/kb/records.jsonl --diagnosed-flag '<flag>' --package '<package>' --gerrit-path '<project>' --category '<category>' --warning-flags '<csv>' --toolchain-profile clang --error-signature '<diagnostic>'
+python -m tizen_campaign_kb kb append --db /work/kb/records.jsonl --record /work/record.json
+python -m tizen_campaign_kb kb promote --db /work/kb/records.jsonl --id '<id>' --to CI_VERIFIED
+python -m tizen_campaign_kb kb import-diff --db /work/kb/records.jsonl --diff /work/fix.diff --ci-log /work/ci.log --package '<package>' --gerrit-path '<project>' --toolchain-profile clang --fix-summary '<summary>' --baseline-commit '<40-hex-source-commit>'
+python -m tizen_campaign_kb campaign-kb-sync --state-db /work/state.db --config /work/campaign.yaml --campaign-unit-key '<key>'
+```
+
+The importer supplies the original source commit, not a blob ID from a diff
+header. Optional `--change-ref` must be a Gerrit change ref; optional
+`--quickbuild-id` records the supplied CI verification provenance. Without it,
+imports are NEW and cannot match T1 or T2. Do not invent CI verification.
+
+## Selection And Synchronization
+
+T1 requires all recorded identity and diagnostic keys to match and a verified
+instance. T2 returns at most the requested limit (default five), with curated
+seed strategies first. `gerrit_url` is display-only; never execute it.
+
+Run sync after the sandbox push and again after the latest QuickBuild result.
+It appends a NEW record, promotes only on PASS, and records KB_SYNC without
+changing campaign state. Repeats are idempotent. The review gate still recomputes
+policy from the bound edit; a KB precedent is not permission to push.
+
+## Failures
+
+Exit 2 is INVALID_ARGS; exit 4 reports KB_SCHEMA_INVALID or state inconsistency.
+Stop on damaged JSONL rather than dropping rows or recreating the database.
+Promotion is monotone. The command performs no build, push or QuickBuild access.
